# Ports and Adapters

Dependencies must point inward.

- Domain code must remain infrastructure-agnostic.
- Application code coordinates use cases and depends on ports.
- Ports represent stable capabilities/contracts.
- Adapters implement ports and own vendor/framework details.
- Composition roots wire concrete dependencies.

Forbidden:

- AWS SDK imports in domain code
- database clients in application/domain business logic
- HTTP request/response objects flowing deep into domain logic
- concrete adapter dependencies in use cases
- circular dependencies across layers

Use interfaces where there is a meaningful boundary or capability.

Do not create interfaces for every class merely to satisfy a style preference.
